    <bpmn:process id="W_W5449" name="W5449. On-Site Debris Collection, Segregation &amp; Load-Out Execution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Crew/ container on site per W5444 dispatch
Frequency: Per cleanup job; daily across crews
Volume: ~thousands of jobs/yr; ~multiple streams per job
Owner: Site Cleanup Crew Lead
Participants: Crew, customer, HSE (VS-24), Dispatch (W5444)
Source: workflow W5449 — On-Site Debris Collection, Segregation &amp; Load-Out Execution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5449_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5449_Lane1" name="Crew Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5449_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5449_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5449_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5449_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5449_Lane2" name="Crew">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5449_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5449_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5449_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5449_Start4" name="Crew/ container on site per W5444 dispatch">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5449_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5449_Task5" name="On arrival, verify site access, JHA/PPE (W5443), container placement permit…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: On arrival, verify site access, JHA/PPE (W5443), container placement permit (W5445), and the work-order scope/exclusions.
Responsible (R): Crew Lead
Accountable (A): Site Cleanup Supervisor
Duration: per job</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5449_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5449_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5449_Task6" name="Segregate debris at load-out into streams: clean wood, drywall…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Segregate debris at load-out into streams: clean wood, drywall, concrete/masonry/tile rubble, metals, packaging/plastic, cardboard, and a separate hazardous-discovery pile.
Responsible (R): Crew
Accountable (A): Crew Lead
Duration: per job</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5449_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5449_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5449_Task7" name="Load container/truck by stream (single-stream mixed if disposal route accepts…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Load container/truck by stream (single-stream mixed if disposal route accepts; multi-stream if diversion targets require separation).
Responsible (R): Crew
Accountable (A): Crew Lead
Duration: per job</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5449_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5449_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5449_Task8" name="Minimize contamination (no food/general waste, no hazardous in mixed C&amp;D) —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Minimize contamination (no food/general waste, no hazardous in mixed C&amp;D) — contaminated loads are rejected by recyclers/landfills and incur surcharges.
Responsible (R): Crew Lead
Accountable (A): Site Cleanup Supervisor
Duration: per job</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5449_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5449_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5449_Task9" name="Capture load photos, stream composition estimate, and time-on-site for the work…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Capture load photos, stream composition estimate, and time-on-site for the work order (W5457).
Responsible (R): Crew Lead
Accountable (A): Site Cleanup Supervisor
Duration: per job</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5449_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5449_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5449_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5449_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-804 (ensure controlled execution — Debris Collection, Segregation &amp; DENR-Compliant Hauling Execution (PA-191.2).) | - operational: stream/load accuracy with no hazardous in mixed C&amp;D; load photos required for every job.
Owner: Site Cleanup Crew Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5449_Assoc12" sourceRef="W5449_Annotation11" targetRef="W5449_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
